  "id": "resting-potential",
  "term": "resting potential",
  "definition": "Resting potential is the baseline electrical state of a neuron when it is not actively firing. In this context, it refers to the membrane voltage that can be slightly shifted by transcranial direct current stimulation, changing cortical excitability.",
